ROG serves as a driver for integrated, ecosystem-based management by bringing multiple sectors and stakeholders together and generating co-benefits for other SDGs.
Successful regional examples (e.g., Micronesia Challenge, CTI-CFF) demonstrate that sustained leadership, consistent donor investment, and long-term capacity development (10–15 years) are critical to transformative outcomes such as establishing marine protected areas and regional monitoring frameworks.
