A short presentation (approximately 10 minutes) intended to stimulate discussion
A brief initial reflection from a designated discussant (approximately 5 minutes)
An open Chatham House discussion among all participants

Four thematic sessions were held:

Improving transparency at sea (Samantha Emmert, Global Fishing Watch)
Lessons learnt from national experiences (Barbara Hutniczak, OECD)
Lessons learnt from Regional Fisheries Management Organisations (Adriana Fabra, Tuna Compliance Network; Hrannar Már Ásgeirsson, NEAFC)
Options for strengthening MCS through a high seas treaty (Klaudija Cremers, IDDRI)

A policy brief was planned for publication following the workshop to disseminate key conclusions.

Key findings
