The European Society for Ecological Economics (ESEE) 16th annual conference (ESEE2026), held at Ghent University (June 30 – July 3, 2026), brings together scholars across ecological economics to advance research and policy dialogue. The program is organized around eleven thematic tracks, including: rethinking wellbeing and prosperity beyond GDP; ecological boundaries and the commons; justice, equity, and inclusive futures; socio-ecological transformation in times of crisis; technology, work, and care; institutional innovation and governance; ecological macroeconomics, public finance, and money; sufficiency, values, and behavioral change; reimagining places and the urban-rural divide; rethinking business and finance; and developments in ecological economics as a scientific field.

Methods
